---@class posthog.error_tracking.MissingSymbolsExample
---@field reason posthog.error_tracking.MissingSymbolsReasonEnum Why the frames miss symbols, as a code. Each code maps to one kind of setup gap. * `chunk_not_uploaded` - Source map not uploaded * `no_source_map_linked` - Script links no source map * `file_not_reachable` - Script or source map not reachable * `invalid_source_map` - Source map URL returns something else * `too_large_to_fetch` - Too large to fetch * `bundle_not_injected` - Bundle not processed by the PostHog CLI * `mapping_not_uploaded` - Mapping file not uploaded * `dsym_not_uploaded` - dSYM not uploaded * `debug_symbols_not_uploaded` - Debug symbols not uploaded
---@field location string|distilled.Null Where the frames come from: the script URL or path, the bundle, or an example class or app image.
---@field symbol_id string|distilled.Null The chunk ID, mapping ID or debug ID that the missing symbols must be uploaded under, when known.
---@field http_status number|distilled.Null The HTTP status the script or source map returned, for 'file_not_reachable'.
---@field frames number How many distinct stack frames in the lookback window this covers.
---@field issues posthog.error_tracking.MissingSymbolsExampleIssuesList Up to five issues whose exceptions in the lookback window contain these frames, most occurrences first.
---@field issue_count number How many issues have exceptions in the lookback window that contain these frames.
---@field issue_count_capped boolean True when the exception scan searched only a sample of the frames or stopped at its limit, so `issue_count` is a lower bound.
---@field example_exception posthog.error_tracking.MissingSymbolsExampleException|distilled.Null A recent exception whose stack trace contains these frames, or null when none was found.

